00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:49.700
Michael Kantor: Yeah, so it is a pretty massive deal. Sorry, I'm just getting my camera on. I've had this cough for the last 2 weeks, and it's been killing me. This is a piece of work that we've been doing and iterating on for the last 4 months with GoDaddy.

70
00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:53.630
Michael Kantor: And, essentially, it's a few things.

71
00:16:54.000 --> 00:17:05.610
Michael Kantor: Number one, GoDaddy has a AI service called the Agent Name Service. It's a DNS-backed way where you can find, identify, and trust AI agents on the internet.

72
00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:15.789
Michael Kantor: ANS is a public specification that is under the IETF. There's a lot of folks who participated in it, GoDaddy, Cisco,

73
00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:35.439
Michael Kantor: I have a number of folks who know OASP as well, so there's a lot of open source foundations there. And the big thing about ANS is it uses something called Merkle trees, which I think many of you are familiar with. But it's kind of like a private system that they've built out internally, and there's no way

74
00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.259
Michael Kantor: there was no way to kind of verify it, so…

75
00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:55.850
Michael Kantor: if the Merkle trees changed, nobody would know about it. And we started working with GoDaddy to essentially create a new standard where you could publish the roots of the Merkle tree on HIRO through the Hedera Consensus Service, and now anyone could actually verify, hey, this…

76
00:17:55.870 --> 00:18:01.440
Michael Kantor: This is the actual root, this is the actual tree, and it hasn't changed.

77
00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:10.849
Michael Kantor: And that's massive for them, right? So they don't have to publish the entire ANS service onto HCS, but they can publish the routes, and now anybody can verify that.

78
00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:18.760
Michael Kantor: So, they've created HCS27, which does that, where you publish those routes, and that'll generate transactions on the network.

79
00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:27.829
Michael Kantor: And they've also created a profile for HCS14, which is our universal agentic ID, and that's a DNS-based way where

80
00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:37.870
Michael Kantor: you can find ANS agents anywhere on the planet in any other registry. For example, at the HOL registry, or ERC 8004, and so forth.

81
00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:55.010
Michael Kantor: This is the start of work. There's additional standards that are also being iterated on in the future. So right now, we publish the routes. The next thing we want to do is being able to actually go and publish each update and record change that an agent has. So today.

82
00:18:55.100 --> 00:19:05.569
Michael Kantor: It's a couple transactions that would happen, and that should go up over time as we work and iterate on this and making ANS verifiable through the Hyrule Consensus service.

